# Mermaid diagrams — mdeai

**Skill (read before editing any ` ```mermaid ` block):** `.claude/skills/mermaid-diagrams/SKILL.md`  
**Required first:** `.claude/skills/mermaid-diagrams/references/best-practices.md`  
**Then one syntax ref** from `references/*.md` matching the diagram type (`load_when` in each file's frontmatter).

## Workflow

1. Pick type → read matching reference (flowchart, sequenceDiagram, journey, erDiagram, …).
2. Author **one idea per diagram** — split if it needs a legend.
3. **Validate** before commit: Mermaid MCP `validate_and_render_mermaid_diagram` or https://mermaid.live; offline gotchas in best-practices §3 if unreachable.
4. Set `verified: YYYY-MM-DD` in the **markdown file** YAML when auditing a diagram set.

## mdeapp stack (Phase 1)

Diagrams for **new work** must match live architecture:

- Next.js 16 · CopilotKit **1.55.2 v1** · Mastra in-process / AG-UI · Gemini · Supabase · Stripe

Do **not** copy legacy nodes from `chatbot-diagrams.md` templates (`ai-chat`, Deno edge, OpenClaw, Vite) into mdeapp docs.

## Syntax traps (top failures)

| Trap | Fix |
|------|-----|
| `end` as flowchart node | Capitalize (`End`) or reword |
| State note inside `state X { }` | Use top-level `note right of X : text` |
| Labels with `()`, `:`, `#` | Quote the label |
| Design tables not migrated | Mark `(design)` in diagram labels; don't imply live schema |
| Client writes to Supabase on approval | Route through server `/api/approval-commit` (see events `03-data-flow.md`) |

## Accessibility (shipped diagram sets)

Inside each mermaid block:

```text
accTitle: Short title
accDescr: One-sentence summary
```

